// This workspace runs on .mjs with JSDoc and emits nothing (AGENTS.md, "No
// TypeScript here, and why"). This file's first duty is the boundary checker's
// import resolution — it is what lets that resolution read modern
// packages: archkeep resolves every specifier through
// `ts.resolveModuleName`, and under typescript 5.x that call with no tsconfig
// runs under default (pre-Node16) settings that cannot read a package
// `exports` map. Measured on this tree with typescript 5.9.3: without this
// file the checker reported six unresolvable imports
// (`vscode-languageclient/node`, `@fast-check/vitest` ×4, `nx/package.json`),
// all exports-map-only entry points; with `module: "nodenext"` all six
// resolve and only the two non-literal dynamic imports remain, which no
// compiler option can fix. Re-measured under typescript 6.0.3 the same probes
// resolve even without these options — 6.0 widened its default resolution —
// but the engine's peer range is `>=5 <7`, so the file earns its keep on the
// 5.x half and stays inert on the 6.x half. `allowJs` and
// `resolveJsonModule` were probed too and changed nothing, so they are absent.
//
// Two further options are stated explicitly because typescript 6.0 flipped
// their defaults to values this workspace never asked for:
//
// - `"strict": false` — 6.0 defaults it to `true`. The programs extending
//   this file were written against the old default on purpose
//   (packages/archkeep/tsconfig.json argues why there is no strict here);
//   leaving the option unstated now means its opposite, and a bump alone
//   turned a green typecheck into ~2,900 strict-mode errors across five
//   programs — measured on this tree. Stating it keeps that decision owned
//   by the workspace rather than inherited from a compiler release.
// - `"types": ["node"]` — 6.0 defaults `types` to `[]`, ending automatic
//   `@types/*` inclusion from node_modules. Every `node:`-prefixed import in
//   a checkJs program then fails as TS2591 — 453 of them across the same
//   run. This names the one type package TS 5 auto-included, restoring the
//   previous program shape exactly.
//
// The engine reads this file through `ts.parseConfigFileTextToJson`
// (packages/archkeep/src/analysis/typescript.mjs), which accepts these
// comments; it uses `compilerOptions` only and ignores include/files globs,
// so neither addition reaches module resolution. The filename is the default
// value of the plugin's `tsConfig` option
// (packages/archkeep/src/options.mjs), so no nx.json change is needed.
//
// The `typecheck` programs — packages/*/tsconfig.json and scripts/tsconfig.json
// — extend this file because their `tsc --noEmit` runs need the same `nodenext`
// resolution; everything they add on top is argued in their own headers.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "nodenext",
    "moduleResolution": "nodenext",
    "strict": false,
    "types": ["node"]
  }
}
